<table>
<tr><th>Scope</th><th>Availability</th><th>Real-life analogy</th></tr>
<tr><td>Request scope</td><td>Only for that one HTTP request; gone when request completes</td><td>Data stored on the HttpServletRequest object</td></tr>
<tr><td>Session scope</td><td>All requests in the same session until logout</td><td>Gmail login — enter username/password once; send 10 mails, check inbox, compose — no re-login until session ends or logout</td></tr>
<tr><td>Application / Context scope</td><td>Entire web application lifetime</td><td>Global shared data</td></tr>
</table>
<table>
<tr><th>Method</th><th>Meaning (thread asks…)</th><th>Returns / effect</th></tr>
<tr><td>`get()`</td><td>&quot;Can you please tell my value?&quot;</td><td>Returns current thread&#x27;s value</td></tr>
<tr><td>`initialValue()`</td><td>&quot;What&#x27;s my initial value?&quot;</td><td>Called internally when no value set yet</td></tr>
<tr><td>`set(newValue)`</td><td>&quot;Can you please set a new value?&quot;</td><td>Stores value for current thread</td></tr>
<tr><td>`remove()`</td><td>&quot;Can you please remove my local variable?&quot;</td><td>Removes current thread&#x27;s entry</td></tr>
</table>
<table>
<tr><th>Topic</th><th>Class</th><th>Key idea</th></tr>
<tr><td>Per-thread local variable</td><td>ThreadLocal</td><td>Separate copy per thread; one object serves all threads</td></tr>
<tr><td>Constructor</td><td>new ThreadLocal()</td><td>Creates the thread-local container</td></tr>
<tr><td>get()</td><td>inherited</td><td>Current thread&#x27;s value</td></tr>
<tr><td>set(v)</td><td>inherited</td><td>Set current thread&#x27;s value</td></tr>
<tr><td>initialValue()</td><td>override optional</td><td>Default null; customize via anonymous subclass</td></tr>
<tr><td>remove()</td><td>Java 1.5+</td><td>Remove current thread&#x27;s entry; next get() re-calls initialValue()</td></tr>
<tr><td>Parent → child inheritance</td><td>InheritableThreadLocal</td><td>Child inherits parent&#x27;s value at thread creation</td></tr>
<tr><td>Custom child value</td><td>childValue(parentValue)</td><td>Override to give child a different value than parent</td></tr>
</table>
